    {
      "id": "item_57",
      "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /workspace/solution/research-notes.md << 'EOF'\n# Research Notes: Single-cell Response Prediction\n\n## Task\nPredict stimulated expression for control cells from an unseen cellular context.\nMetric: MSE of per-gene mean predicted vs true stimulated expression (lower is better).\nBaseline anchor B = 0.003657 (initial VAE method).\nScore = (B - MSE) / B (higher is better).\n\n## Method Architecture\nStatistical cell-type reference ensemble with power-law modulation:\n1. Per-cell-type control means and stimulated diffs from training data\n2. Target context cell-type weights via softmax of Spearman correlations\n3. Consensus shrinkage based on cross-cell-type disagreement of stim diffs\n4. Power-law scaling: scaled_diff = ref_diff * (target_ctrl / ref_ctrl) ** pow_gene\n5. Per-gene power varies by expression quantile\n6. Ensemble over multiple temperatures and power configs\n\n## Experiment History\n\n### v39 (baseline) - Dev MSE = 0.001871, Score = 0.4882\n- Initial cell-type reference ensemble method\n- No ratio modulation\n\n### v51/v53 - progression through various improvements\n- Added quantile-dependent power\n- Added shrinkage based on cross-cell-type disagreement\n- Added ratio modulation for up-genes\n\n### v56 (best scored) - Dev MSE = 0.001607, Score = 0.5604\n- RATIO_MOD_UP = 0.03 (signed log-ratio modulation for up-genes only)\n- ENSEMBLE_TEMPS = [0.05, 0.07, 0.09], weights [0.3, 0.4, 0.3]\n- UP_POWER_CONFIGS = [(0.80, -0.55), (1.00, -0.65), (1.20, -0.85)]\n- BASE_DOWN_POW = 1.40, SLOPE_DOWN_POW = -0.75\n- UP_SHRINK_STRENGTH = 0.5, DOWN_SHRINK_STRENGTH = 0.0\n- File: method_v57_worse.py (hash: f66fa308)\n- Recorded in recovered-own-dev.json\n\n### v57_test (untested) - RATIO_MOD_UP = 0.01\n- Lower ratio modulation for up-genes\n- File: method_v57_test.py (hash: 86c9e999)\n\n### v58 (pending - GPU outage) - RATIO_MOD_UP = 0.01, RATIO_MOD_DOWN = 0.01\n- Added signed log-ratio modulation for down-genes\n- Rationale: symmetric modulation for both up and down genes\n- If target has higher expression (ratio > 1), both up and down regulation should be stronger\n- Current method.py\nEOF\necho \\\"Research notes created\\\"\"",
      "original_command_sha256": "5348bdec17ce0726bd48fcf86d5850fe4973724d71030724ddf7b2cc099426d8",
      "command_email_identifiers_redacted": true,
      "exit_code": 0,
      "output_sha256": "f470b886148bd7946d5407e44076a8fb600cfe441e3abb19980c06691d422cf6",
      "output_characters": 23
